    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1079">

                <pb facs="0915" n="799" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg799"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3674.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        Manuel L. Luján to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As delegate from General Pascual Orozco, commander in chief of the Mexican
                    revolutionary army, I beg to convey to you the respects of General Orozco.
                    Should the United States Government see fit to honor General Orozco with any
                    communication I, as his representative, with full powers, am instructed to
                    receive such communication and to make known to you my place of residence in
                    this country. I shall be honored to present to your excellency my personal
                    respects and credentials whenever your Government feels so disposed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel L. Luján</hi></signed>, <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">225 West 80th St., New York City, N. Y.</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
